# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dev.to publishing config  --  EXAMPLE / TEMPLATE
#
#   cp .config/devto.config.example .config/devto.config
#   then edit .config/devto.config and paste your real key
#
# .config/devto.config is gitignored. This .example file is safe to commit
# because it contains no real secrets. Never put a real key in this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Your DEV Community API key.
#
# Where to get it:
#   1. Log in to https://dev.to
#   2. Go to https://dev.to/settings/extensions
#        (or: click your avatar -> Settings -> "Extensions" in the left sidebar)
#   3. Scroll to the BOTTOM of that page, to "DEV Community API Keys"
#   4. Type a description, e.g.  DailyKodePractice CLI
#   5. Click "Generate API Key"
#   6. Copy the key that appears and paste it below
#
# The key is shown in the list after generation, so you can copy it again later.
# If it ever leaks, delete it on that same page and generate a new one.
#
DEVTO_API_KEY=paste_your_key_here


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the publisher looks for the key (in order, first match wins)
#
#   1.  export DEVTO_API_KEY=<key>       environment variable, good for CI
#   2.  $DEVTO_API_KEY_FILE              path to a file holding just the key
#   3.  .config/devto.config             this file  <-- the default
#   4.  ~/.config/devto/config           same format, outside the repo entirely
#
# Prefer 4 if you would rather no secret ever sits inside a git working tree,
# even a gitignored one:
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/devto
#   cp .config/devto.config.example ~/.config/devto/config
#   chmod 600 ~/.config/devto/config
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
